---
// The Switch page (cl_audit after 26.11.0, app build 252), as the app shows it in its window instead of the dashboard:
// the account in use and the one to switch to, what stays, what follows (Sessions follow), and the steps with their
// keys. The demo switches "work" to its standby account "team-2"; dashboard.astro runs the steps with sample timings
// (nothing on this Mac changes). Sample addresses and counts only.
import { accounts, standby, shortName } from "../data/demo";

const a = accounts.find((x) => x.id === "work")!;
const s = standby.work[0];
const from = shortName(a.email), to = shortName(s.email);
---
<section class="sw-page" data-sw-page hidden aria-label={`Switch Claude ${a.name} to ${to}`}>
  <div class="sw-head">
    <h3>Switch Claude {a.name} to {to}</h3>
    <span class="disp xs">{from} <em>→ {to}</em></span>
  </div>
  <div class="sw-cols">
    <div class="sw-col">
      <div class="card"><h4>Accounts <i class="idot" title={`The account ${a.name} works on now, and the one it would switch to, with their limits as cl_audit last read them.`}>i</i></h4>
        <div class="acc-list">
          <div class="abox"><div class="abox-head"><i class="abox-lamp on"></i><span class="abox-t"><b class="email" data-sw-in-mail>{a.email}</b><small data-sw-in-plan>{a.plan} · Work</small></span><span class="disp xs abox-badge"><span class="g">In use</span></span></div><div data-sw-in-limits></div></div>
          <div class="abox"><div class="abox-head"><i class="abox-lamp"></i><span class="abox-t"><b class="email" data-sw-to-mail>{s.email}</b><small data-sw-to-plan>{s.plan} · {s.org}</small></span><span class="disp xs abox-badge" data-sw-to-badge>Switch to</span></div><div data-sw-to-limits></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Stays as it is <i class="idot" title={`Switching changes only the account ${a.name} works on. Everything that makes it ${a.name} stays.`}>i</i></h4>
        <div class="srow"><span>Profile</span><span class="v-soft">Name, Dock icon, look</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Folder</span><span class="v-soft">{a.dir}: projects, settings, MCP, CLAUDE.md</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>History</span><span class="v-soft">Claude Code's, for claude --resume</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sw-col">
      <div class="card"><h4>Follows to {to} <i class="idot" title={`With Sessions follow on (Settings ▸ ${a.name} ▸ Claude Code), the Claude window's Code sidebar goes with the account: its sessions, sections and groups, pins and scheduled tasks, so the window opens the same. They come back when ${a.name} switches back. Chats and Projects on claude.ai belong to each account and don't move.`}>i</i></h4>
        <div class="srow"><span>Sessions</span><span class="v-soft">14 sessions in the sidebar (and 3 archived)</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Sidebar</span><span class="v-soft">2 sections, 3 groups and the pins</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Routines</span><span class="v-soft">2 scheduled tasks</span></div>
        <p class="g-note sub">Chats and Projects on claude.ai don't move; they belong to each account.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Steps <i class="idot" title="What switching does, in order. Each step is checked before the next. A receipt in cl_audit's folder keeps what moved: until Claude Code has signed in, Cancel puts it back; after that the way back is a switch the other way.">i</i></h4>
        <ol class="sw-steps" data-sw-steps>
          <li data-step="1"><i></i><div><b>{a.name}'s Claude window closes</b><span>Only that window, for about half a minute; your other Claude windows stay open.</span></div></li>
          <li data-step="2"><i></i><div><b>The sessions move to {to}</b><span>Same ids; nothing is copied. Their groups and pins are noted for step 5.</span></div></li>
          <li data-step="3"><i></i><div><b data-step3-t>Claude Code and the window sign in as {to}</b><span data-step3-d>Claude Code in Terminal and the browser, then the window's own sign-in.</span></div></li>
          <li data-step="4"><i></i><div><b>{a.name} works on {to}</b><span>Its numbers then are {to}'s; {from} waits on standby.</span></div></li>
          <li data-step="5"><i></i><div><b>The sidebar, as before</b><span data-step5-d>Press Return in the session that opens, so the sidebar is arranged as before.</span></div></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="sw-keys" data-sw-keys></div>
        <p class="g-note sub sw-line" data-sw-line hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- the yes before it starts, as the app's alert -->
  <div class="dialog-veil" data-sw-confirm hidden>
    <div class="dialog" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="sw-c-title">
      <b id="sw-c-title">Switch Claude {a.name} to {to}?</b>
      <p>{a.name}'s Claude window closes. Its 17 sessions and 2 scheduled tasks move to {to}, with a receipt to undo it. Then Claude Code signs in as {to} in Terminal and the browser, and the window opens for its own sign-in. Once it's on {to}, a session opens there to arrange the sidebar: press Return in it.</p>
      <p class="sub">This is a demo: nothing on your Mac changes.</p>
      <div class="dialog-btns sw-c-btns"><button type="button" class="pill small" data-sw-no>Cancel</button><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sw-yes>Close and switch</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
